hi I'm Emily Ekins and I'm the polling  director at Reason Foundation we  recently conducted a poll of Americans  on landlines and cellphones asking them  questions about government spending the  debt ceiling gun control and drug reform  I'd like to tell you about some of the  results we have several questions about  government spending the federal budget  deficit and the debt ceiling we found  sixty-four percent of americans oppose  raising the debt ceiling one of the  reasons is that only a quarter think  that failing to raise the debt ceiling  would actually result in an economic  crisis since 1990 federal government  spending per person has increased  thirty-nine percent adjusted for  inflation we found that only seventeen  percent of Americans felt that this  increased spending had improved their  quality of life this helps explain why  only twelve percent of americans think  that rolling spending levels back to the  1990s levels would hurt the economy we  asked a number of questions about drug  policy we found that republicans  democrats and independents all agree  that the federal government should not  get involved in states that have  legalized the recreational use of  marijuana for instance republicans  democrats and independents all agree  that the federal government should not  arrest individuals who use grow or sell  marijuana in the states that have  legalized it in light of new proposals  for gun legislation we asked a number of  questions about gun control first we  found that 51 percent of americans  believe that individuals should be  allowed to own assault weapons  forty-four percent disagree and believe  they should be prohibited we asked  Americans if they thought the assault  weapons ban would have prevented the  shooter in Newtown Connecticut had the  law still been in effect we found that  only twenty-seven percent of Americans  felt like it would we asked them why and  of these Americans they felt it would  have prevented the shooter from  obtaining the weapons that he used this  is particularly interesting given that  Connecticut already has an assault  weapons ban on the books and the weapons  that lambs are used were legal under  state law to learn more about what  Americans think about entitlement reform  cutting defense spending taxes and more  please visit reason.com forward slash  poll  you
 

